.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef struct \fBp8est_iter_corner_info\fP \fBp8est_iter_corner_info_t\fP"

.PP
The information that is available to the user-defined p8est_iter_corner_t callback\&. If tree_boundary is false, the corner is on the interior of a tree\&. When tree_boundary is false, sides[0] contains the lowest z-order quadrant that touches the corner\&. When tree_boundary is true, its value is P8EST_CONNECT_FACE/EDGE/CORNER depending on the location of the corner relative to the tree\&. 
.SS "typedef void(* p8est_iter_corner_t) (\fBp8est_iter_corner_info_t\fP *info, void *user_data)"

.PP
The prototype for a function that p8est_iterate will execute wherever the corner is a corner for all quadrants that touch it\&. i\&.e\&. the callback will not execute on a corner that sits on a hanging face or edge\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinfo\fP information about a quadrant provided to the user 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP the user context passed to \fBp8est_iterate()\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
the forest does not need to be corner balanced for \fBp8est_iterate()\fP to execute a callback function at corners, only face and edge balanced\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "typedef struct \fBp8est_iter_edge_info\fP \fBp8est_iter_edge_info_t\fP"

.PP
The information about all sides of an edge in the forest\&. If tree_boundary is false, the edge is on the interior of a tree\&. When tree_boundary is false, sides[0] contains the lowest z-order quadrant that touches the edge\&. When tree_boundary is true, its value is P8EST_CONNECT_FACE/EDGE depending on the location of the edge relative to the tree\&. 
.SS "typedef void(* p8est_iter_edge_t) (\fBp8est_iter_edge_info_t\fP *info, void *user_data)"

.PP
The prototype for a function that p8est_iterate will execute wherever the edge is an edge of all quadrants that touch it i\&.e\&. the callback will not execute on an edge the sits on a hanging face\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinfo\fP information about a quadrant provided to the user 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP the user context passed to \fBp8est_iterate()\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
the forest must be edge balanced for \fBp8est_iterate()\fP to execute a callback function on edges\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "typedef struct \fBp8est_iter_face_info\fP \fBp8est_iter_face_info_t\fP"

.PP
The information that is available to the user-defined p8est_iter_face_t callback\&. The orientation is 0 if the face is within one tree; otherwise, it is the same as the orientation value between the two trees given in the connectivity\&. If the face is on the outside of the forest, then there is only one side\&. If tree_boundary is false, the face is on the interior of a tree\&. When tree_boundary false, sides[0] contains the lowest z-order quadrant that touches the face\&. When tree_boundary is true, its value is P8EST_CONNECT_FACE\&. 
.SS "typedef struct \fBp8est_iter_face_side\fP \fBp8est_iter_face_side_t\fP"

.PP
Information about one side of a face in the forest\&. If a \fIquad\fP is local (\fIis_ghost\fP is false), then its \fIquadid\fP indexes the tree's quadrant array; otherwise, it indexes the ghosts array\&. If the face is hanging, then the quadrants are listed in z-order\&. If a quadrant should be present, but it is not included in the ghost layer, then quad = NULL, is_ghost is true, and quadid = -1\&. 
.SS "typedef void(* p8est_iter_face_t) (\fBp8est_iter_face_info_t\fP *info, void *user_data)"

.PP
The prototype for a function that \fBp8est_iterate()\fP will execute wherever two quadrants share a face: the face can be a 2:1 hanging face, it does not have to be conformal\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinfo\fP information about a quadrant provided to the user 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP the user context passed to \fBp8est_iterate()\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
the forest must be face balanced for \fBp8est_iterate()\fP to execute a callback function on faces (see \fBp8est_balance()\fP)\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "typedef struct \fBp8est_iter_volume_info\fP \fBp8est_iter_volume_info_t\fP"

.PP
The information that is available to the user-defined p8est_iter_volume_t callback function\&. \fItreeid\fP gives the index in \fIp4est->trees\fP of the tree to which \fIquad\fP belongs\&. \fIquadid\fP gives the index of \fIquad\fP within \fItree's\fP quadrants array\&. 
.SS "typedef void(* p8est_iter_volume_t) (\fBp8est_iter_volume_info_t\fP *info, void *user_data)"

.PP
The prototype for a function that \fBp8est_iterate()\fP will execute at every quadrant local to the current process\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinfo\fP information about a quadrant provided to the user 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP the user context passed to \fBp8est_iterate()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void p8est_iterate (\fBp8est_t\fP * p4est, \fBp8est_ghost_t\fP * ghost_layer, void * user_data, \fBp8est_iter_volume_t\fP iter_volume, \fBp8est_iter_face_t\fP iter_face, \fBp8est_iter_edge_t\fP iter_edge, \fBp8est_iter_corner_t\fP iter_corner)"

.PP
Execute the user-supplied callback functions at every volume, face, edge and corner in the local forest\&. The ghost_layer may be NULL\&. The \fIuser_data\fP pointer is not touched by p8est_iterate, but is passed to each of the callbacks\&. Any of the callback functions may be NULL\&. The callback functions are interspersed with each other, i\&.e\&. some face callbacks will occur between volume callbacks, and some edge callbacks will occur between face callbacks, etc\&.:
.PP
1) volume callbacks occur in the sorted Morton-index order\&. 2) a face callback is not executed until after the volume callbacks have been executed for the quadrants that share it\&. 3) an edge callback is not executed until the face callbacks have been executed for all faces that touch the edge\&. 4) a corner callback is not executed until the edge callbacks have been executed for all edges that touch the corner\&. 5) it is not always the case that every face callback for a given quadrant is executed before any of the edge or corner callbacks, and it is not always the case that every edge callback for a given quadrant is executed before any of the corner callbacks\&. 6) callbacks are not executed at faces, edges or corners that only involve ghost quadrants, i\&.e\&. that are not adjacent in the local section of the forest\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fI\fBp4est\fP\fP the forest 
.br
\fIghost_layer\fP optional: when not given, callbacks at the boundaries of the local partition cannot provide quadrant data about ghost quadrants: missing (p8est_quadrant_t *) pointers are set to NULL, missing indices are set to -1\&. 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP optional context to supply to each callback 
.br
\fIiter_volume\fP callback function for every quadrant's interior 
.br
\fIiter_face\fP callback function for every face between quadrants 
.br
\fIiter_edge\fP callback function for every edge between quadrants 
.br
\fIiter_corner\fP callback function for every corner between quadrants 
.RE
.PP

